  "notes": "Mariah Carey's Crave label girl group: Trackmasters-orbit hip-hop soul with 80s freestyle interpolations, 1997–2001. The research gives \"70–103 straight; ballads 70–88\" with five sourced tempos, so the mode sits at 96 and `halfTime` is false. Three drum deltas from \"sampled boom-bap loop with a clap doubling 2&4, 16th hats thin, and the source record's own drums audible underneath\": a clap stacked 3–8 ms off the snare (the widest offset in this batch, which is what \"audible underneath\" sounds like), a snare pushed 3–8 ms off the grid with `quantizeStrength` at 0.62, and a continuous 16th hat at only 0.2 fill density. Harmony is \"80s freestyle/quiet-storm harmony inherited from the covered material — 4-chord minor cycles\", so the families are four-chord minor rather than the lane's two-chord vamps. \"Four-part group harmony, and a guest-rap or guest-vocal foil as the arrangement's second voice\" is the high chord-tone bias and a counter at +12. The low end is \"the interpolated source bassline carries the low end; kick reinforcement beneath it\", so there is no `bass808` block and the bass follows roots at 0.8 with a modest passing-tone set. ⚠ Confidence is **low**: the research rates the entry medium-low and marks the key claim `[LOW-CONF]` — the keys follow the interpolated source, which is not named, so they are lane-level here. ⚠ Every velocity, density and register number is INFERRED.",
